 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-1000) 'Where the organization digit comes from
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-1000) 'The digit is a short name for an arc under an IANA Private Enterprise Number.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-1000) 'PEN 66606 is assigned to iFire. RFC 9371 gives the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-1000) 'registration procedure, and the assignment is itself the delegation. No arc
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-1000) 'below 66606 is registered with anybody.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-1000) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-1000) 'That is also the hazard. RFC 9371 section 1.1 says plainly that no one controls
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-1000) 'how an assignee uses its PEN. Nothing outside this workspace will stop two of
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-1000) 'our own namespaces from minting the same arc. Only a table we keep will.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-1000) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-1000) 'So one arc under the PEN names a namespace, and no namespace mints a sibling of
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-1000) 'another:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1000  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-1000) '
 # tags: rfd:details
